  "body": "When parity error detection is enabled it is unclear how this should be communicated to a client using the ReadableStream interface. Unlike the errors that can be encountered in the response body of a `fetch()` these are not fatal. The options as I see it,\r\n\r\n1. Ignore errors.\r\n1. Halt the ReadableStream when  an error is detected and require the error to be explicitly cleared to open a new stream that will receive the next byte after the error.\r\n1. Signal errors in-band using a mechanism similar to the PARMRK flag on POSIX systems. The application will need to inspect the input byte by byte to separate errors from the actual data.",
